Description: Hyprland: use the -m and -w paths for every file
 nwg-displays 0.5.0 takes the Hyprland monitor and workspace files from its
 -m/--monitors_path and -w/--workspaces_path options when it saves, but three
 other places name ~/.config/hypr/monitors.conf and workspaces.conf directly:
 the module creates both files, empty, when it is imported (main.py, before
 the options are parsed); the mirror check in list_outputs() reads mirror
 lines from monitors.conf (tools.py); and the workspaces window loads the
 workspace rules from workspaces.conf (main.py, create_workspaces_window_hypr).
 Started with other paths, nwg-displays left two empty files under
 ~/.config/hypr, saw no mirror it had saved, and opened the workspaces window
 empty after workspaces had been saved. The patch creates the files at the
 -m and -w paths once the options are parsed, and passes those paths to the
 mirror check and the workspaces window. Started with no options, the paths
 are the defaults, so nothing changes.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-22
